              "textField": "Hypertension is a major contributing factor to the development of atherosclerosis, but it can also cause aneurysms, headaches, and other problems. When testing blood pressure, there is a high number associated with ventricular contraction called the *systolic* blood pressure and a lower blood pressure called the *diastolic* blood pressure. Factors that affect blood pressure include *physical factors* such as the elastic properties of the blood vessels and the narrowing of the blood vessels. They also include *physiologic factors* such as cardiac output, peripheral vascular resistance. Most of our therapies for blood pressure will be targeting the physiologic factors."
